From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shawn-makes-stuff <shawn.rains@rocketmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 03:32:54 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 14/22] firmware: the HiFi4 DSP (COSMOS 0006) in Rust

The CC1's mainboard MCU: src/hifi4 (the board, RPMsg over the msgbox, the
resource table, the trace log, startup and vectors as global_asm!) and
src/hifi4/lib (the lib/hifi4 drivers it calls: hal_core, ccu, gpio, gpadc,
msgbox, watchdog).

- targets/xtensa-hifi4-none-elf.json: Espressif's xtensa LLVM (toolchain
  esp), the call0 ABI, the core options COSMOS's gcc uses; links with
  COSMOS's Zephyr gcc and its linker script (build/hifi4.ld, literals
  before code)
- build: the hifi4 sources; requests in source order (the C build is -O0)
- configs/cosmos-cc1-dsp (config.mainboard): requests + dictionary
  identical to the C build, whose dictionary equals the printer's; the
  resource table is byte-identical; ctr_check 72/72 on all configs
- rusticc/deploy/dsp-test.sh + mcu_identify.py: load it on the printer by
  hand from /user-resource/rusticc and read its dictionary (not run yet)

